 "solutions": [
  {
   "question": "5",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "The graph is translated 1 unit left, reflected in the $x$-axis and dilated vertically by a factor of 2. Key points on the sketch: $(-3,0)$, $(-2,-2)$, $(-1,0)$, $(2,0)$.\n\n\\exfigure{175_q5_s1}",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "6",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$$y = \\sqrt{x-3}$$ $$y = \\sqrt{2x-3}$$ $$y = \\sqrt{2x-3} - 1$$ $$y = 4\\left(\\sqrt{2x-3} - 1\\right) = 4\\sqrt{2x-3} - 4$$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "7",
   "part": "a",
   "latex": "$y = \\tan\\left(2x - \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\tan\\left[2\\left(x - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right]$\n\nHorizontal dilation of scale factor $\\dfrac{1}{2}$.\n\nHorizontal translation $\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ to the right.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "7",
   "part": "b",
   "latex": "Period for $\\tan(ax)$ is $\\dfrac{\\pi}{a} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "8",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$2\\cos x = -\\sqrt{3}$\n\n$\\cos x = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\n\n$\\cos$ is negative in Q2 and Q3.\n\n$\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$\n\n$x = \\pi - \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$ in Q2, $\\pi + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$ in Q3\n\n$x = \\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}, \\dfrac{7\\pi}{6}$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "9",
   "part": "a",
   "latex": "$u = 3x^2 + 4$, $y = u^5$\n\n$\\dfrac{du}{dx} = 6x$, $\\dfrac{dy}{du} = 5u^4$\n\n$\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = 6x \\times 5(3x^2+4)^4 = 30x(3x^2+4)^4$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "9",
   "part": "b",
   "latex": "$u = \\cos x$, $v = x^2$, $u' = -\\sin x$, $v' = 2x$\n\n$\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = \\dfrac{vu' - uv'}{v^2} = \\dfrac{-x^2\\sin x - 2x\\cos x}{x^4} = \\dfrac{-x(x\\sin x + 2\\cos x)}{x^4} = -\\dfrac{x\\sin x + 2\\cos x}{x^3}$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "9",
   "part": "c",
   "latex": "$\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\cdot\\dfrac{f'(x)}{f(x)} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\times\\dfrac{2x}{x^2} = \\dfrac{1}{x}$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "10",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$f(x) = x^4 - 2x^3 + 5x + C$\n\n$10 = (1)^4 - 2(1)^3 + 5(1) + C$\n\n$10 = 1 - 2 + 5 + C$, so $C = 6$\n\n$f(x) = x^4 - 2x^3 + 5x + 6$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "11",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$f'(x) = 2\\cos 2x - 3$\n\nRange of $2\\cos 2x$ is $[-2, 2]$.\n\nRange of $2\\cos 2x - 3$ is $[-5, -1]$.\n\nAll values of $f'(x) < 0$, so it is a decreasing function.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "12",
   "part": "a",
   "latex": "$SA = 2x^2 + 4xh$\n\n$294 = 2x^2 + 4xh$\n\n$4xh = 294 - 2x^2$\n\n$h = \\dfrac{294 - 2x^2}{4x} = \\dfrac{2(147 - x^2)}{4x} = \\dfrac{147 - x^2}{2x}$\n\n$V = x^2h = x^2\\left(\\dfrac{147 - x^2}{2x}\\right) = \\dfrac{147x - x^3}{2}$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "12",
   "part": "b",
   "latex": "$V = \\dfrac{147x}{2} - \\dfrac{x^3}{2}$\n\n$\\dfrac{dV}{dx} = \\dfrac{147}{2} - \\dfrac{3x^2}{2}$\n\n$\\dfrac{d^2V}{dx^2} = -\\dfrac{6x}{2} = -3x$\n\nStationary point when $\\dfrac{dV}{dx} = 0$:\n\n$\\dfrac{147}{2} - \\dfrac{3x^2}{2} = 0$\n\n$147 - 3x^2 = 0$\n\n$3(49 - x^2) = 0$\n\n$3(7+x)(7-x) = 0$\n\n$x = 7$ ($x > 0$)\n\nWhen $x = 7$, $\\dfrac{d^2V}{dx^2} = -3\\times 7 = -21 < 0$ so a maximum.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
